**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests`

**How to implement.** The study as Domain data, and CreateStudy's pure half (001 §L '`Study` grows from the experiment collection: a named set of experiments inside ONE kit, plus: the unknowns (owner + scope); sessions; fit settings; its append-only fit runs', the scope table, 'Weights and ablation: a weight per experiment or per detector; enable / disable per experiment'; 001 §E 'notes on … studies … live in their files'; 001 §P `CreateStudy`; the S11.1 brief). Fit runs are their own files (S11.3). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. Every case name has two words and no `bool` appears. In `Studies.fs`, after `StudySession` (step 357), in this order: (1) `StudyName of string` with `.value`, `static member tryCreate (text : string) : Result<StudyName, StudyError>` keeping the text and refusing an empty or white-space one with `InvalidStudyNameErr`, and `member this.fileStem : FileStem` = `FileStem.ofText this.value` (step 24), the stem of its `<name>.study-json` (001 §A). (2) `StudyNotes of string` with `.value` and `static member none`. (3) `ParameterScope` = `ItemScope` | `MaterialScope` | `SessionBlockScope` | `ExperimentScope` (001 §L 'Scope is the sharing rule'): `member this.value : int` 1 to 4 in that order, `static member tryOfWire (tag : int) : ParameterScope option`, `member this.text : string` (`Item`, `Material`, `Session`, `Experiment`) and `static member all`. The session case is `SessionBlockScope`, after 001's 'one value per session block', because STL declares a `SessionScope` case and DU case names are unique among ours (AGENTS.md, ELEV016; the lower assembly keeps its name). (4) `StudyParameterRef` = `ItemParameterRef of item : ItemId * name : ParameterName` | `MaterialParameterRef of material : MaterialVersionId * name : ParameterName`, with `member this.name : ParameterName` and `member this.describe : string` (`item <GUID> <name>` or `material <GUID> v<n> <name>`). (5) `ScopedParameter = { parameter : StudyParameterRef; scope : ParameterScope }`, a scope the study sets. (6) `ParameterLink = { follower : StudyParameterRef; leader : StudyParameterRef }`, 'CPL2.δ = CPL1.δ': the follower takes the leader's value (001 §L 'Explicit links … are constraints'). (7) `SessionGainSetting = { session : SessionName; model : SessionGainModel }`. (8) `FitMode` = `JointFit` | `StagedFit` (001 §L 'Fit modes'; S11.3 runs them), with `value` 1-2, `tryOfWire`, `text` (`Joint`, `Staged`) and `all`. (9) `ResidualWeight of float` with `.value`, `static member tryCreate (value : float) : Result<ResidualWeight, StudyError>` refusing a NaN, infinite, zero or negative value with `InvalidResidualWeightErr`, and `static member unit` (1.0). (10) `ExperimentWeightSetting = { experiment : ExperimentName; weight : ResidualWeight }` and `DetectorWeightSetting = { detector : ItemId; weight : ResidualWeight }`. (11) `StudyFitSettings = { mode : FitMode; experimentWeights : ExperimentWeightSetting list; detectorWeights : DetectorWeightSetting list; disabled : ExperimentName list }`, with `static member initial` (`JointFit`, no weight, nothing disabled). (12) `OpenedMaterial = { version : MaterialVersionId; name : EntryName; crystal : CrystalParameters; parameters : Parameter list }`, the study-local working copy of an opened material version (001 §I 'a study OPENS a material version, which creates a study-local working copy, stored in the study file'), which step 361 fills. (13) `Study = { name : StudyName; experiments : ExperimentName list; materials : OpenedMaterial list; scopes : ScopedParameter list; links : ParameterLink list; sessionGains : SessionGainSetting list; settings : StudyFitSettings; notes : StudyNotes }`. Experiments are named by `ExperimentName`, because a kit stores each under its name (step 290). (14) `static member create (name : StudyName) (experiments : ExperimentName list) (held : Study list) (kitExperiments : Experiment list) : Result<Study, StudyError>`: `DuplicateStudyNameErr` naming both when a held study's `name.fileStem` equals the name's ignoring case (every `<name>.study-json` shares the kit root, step 216's rule for items); `UnknownStudyExperimentErr` naming the first name no kit experiment has; otherwise the study holding the names in order, each once, with nothing opened, scoped or linked, no gain setting, `StudyFitSettings.initial` and `StudyNotes.none`. (15) `member this.sessionsIn (kitExperiments : Experiment list) : StudySession list`: `StudySession.splitAll` of the study's experiments as `kitExperiments` holds them, in study order. (16) `member this.gainModelOf (session : SessionName) : SessionGainModel`: the setting's model, or `FreeSessionGain`. `StudyError` gains `InvalidStudyNameErr` (`the study name is not valid: <reason>`), `DuplicateStudyNameErr` (`the kit already has a study of that name: <reason>`), `UnknownStudyExperimentErr` (`the kit has no such experiment: <reason>`) and `InvalidResidualWeightErr` (`the residual weight is not valid: <reason>`). No wire converter is added here: the study file (step 359) adds the two. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs`, `module StudyTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over test-local experiments built as in `StudySessionTests`: `a study name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`: `StudyName.tryCreate "QZ:LR"` keeps the text and its `fileStem` is `FileStem "QZ_LR"`, and `""` and `"  "` answer `InvalidStudyNameErr`; `a parameter scope and a fit mode round-trip their wire tags and render their text`: the tags 1-4 and 1-2 in order, `tryOfWire` inverse to `value`, `None` for 0 and 5 (and 3), the texts as above and `all` in tag order; `a residual weight refuses a non-finite or non-positive value`: 0.5 and 2 are kept, and NaN, +∞, 0 and −1 answer `InvalidResidualWeightErr`; `a study is created over the kit's experiments in order, each once, with the initial settings, and refuses a held name or an experiment the kit lacks`: over E1, E2 and E3, `create` of `QZ-LR` with [E2; E1; E2] answers [E2; E1] with the initial settings; with a held study `qz-lr` it answers `DuplicateStudyNameErr`; with [E1; E9] `UnknownStudyExperimentErr` naming E9; `a study's sessions split its experiments in study order, and a session without a setting has a free gain`: a study of [E3; D1; E1] (D1 Diagnostic) answers `Session 1` [E3] and `Session 2` [E1], and `gainModelOf` of each is `FreeSessionGain`. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the four new cases.

**Acceptance.** After the study's shape lands, `Studies.fs` MUST declare `StudyName`, `StudyNotes`, `ParameterScope` (with `SessionBlockScope`), `StudyParameterRef`, `ScopedParameter`, `ParameterLink`, `SessionGainSetting`, `FitMode`, `ResidualWeight`, the weight settings, `StudyFitSettings`, `OpenedMaterial` and `Study`, and `Study.create` MUST refuse a held name and an unknown experiment; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a study name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`, `a parameter scope and a fit mode round-trip their wire tags and render their text`, `a residual weight refuses a non-finite or non-positive value`, `a study is created over the kit's experiments in order, each once, with the initial settings, and refuses a held name or an experiment the kit lacks` and `a study's sessions split its experiments in study order, and a session without a setting has a free gain`, the count rising by 5, and the widened `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.
